# AgentRef — environment reference
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in only what you need. The app ships pointing at
# the DEPLOYED GenLayer Intelligent Contract on Studio Dev — chain 61997
# (src/core/genlayer/contract.ts → LIVE_CONTRACT), so READING the on-chain
# verdict works with no configuration at all.
#
# Env is read in src/core/genlayer/config.ts (client-safe) and
# src/core/genlayer/runtime.ts (server-only).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GenLayer — the REAL validator path
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The app targets GenLayer **Studio Dev** (chain 61997), contract
# 0xaF982d37492368e03413DaCe68E8525bf97f822B. Defaults already point there, so
# both lines below are OPTIONAL overrides — set them only to target your own
# deployment:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AGENTREF_CONTRACT_ADDRESS=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AGENTREF_NETWORK=studio_dev   # studio_dev (default) | localnet
#
# genlayer-js/chains exports are camelCase, so the network label maps to the
# right chain export automatically (studio_dev → studioDevnet) and you normally
# do NOT need the next line. Set it only to force a different export:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AGENTREF_CHAIN_KEY=studioDevnet

# Server-only signer for the WRITE path (create_receipt → challenge →
# adjudicate). NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_, never commit, never expose to
# the client. Must be a 0x-prefixed 64-hex private key **funded on Studio Dev**
# — test GEN does not carry across networks, so a key funded on another chain
# still needs funds on chain 61997. Without it the app can still READ the
# shared on-chain verdict; it just cannot sign new adjudications.
#
# AGENTBEE_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY is checked FIRST; AGENTREF_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY is
# the older name and is still honoured, so existing deployments keep signing.
# AGENTBEE_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY=
# AGENTREF_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY=
# AGENTREF_ACCOUNT_NAME=agentref
